=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=
Reboot release. And a BIT cleaned.
Watch this E! Sysops :

I and another E! sysop noticed a bug.. it's more in E! then in
my door. If you change the text in the language file, E! doens't
accept a space after the text. So DON'T use ED.. use another
texteditor, who can see "free space" on a line.
So NO spaces behind \n1\q1\#0Doors:Num/Num1.0LOGOUT

The line must end after the character "T" from logout !!!!

If you still can't understand this, or still having problems,
then mail me! 
=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=

1. The Door
~~~~~~~~~~~
This is a Next User Message door ;)
So just before a user logs off, they can write a short
message for the next user(s) until another user has changed it.
And the message will be displayed when a users logs on...

2. Why ?
~~~~~~~~
I made this door, because I missed it :)
When I was running on MaxsBBS (Ulgh) I had also a NUM like door..
it was called Magic Next v2.0 I thought...

3. Files
~~~~~~~~ 
In this archive there are 6 files !
                          ~
- NUM1.01LOGOUT
- NUM1.01LOGIN  
- Num.doc
- Num.msg
- Important.notes
- File_id.diz

If these aren't in the archive, then there is a lamer which
deleted some files.. if there are more.. hehe.. then those are
just bbsadds, I hope :)

4. Installation
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
First you must assign DOORS:
But I think you already had that one assigned! :)
Then you must create a directory called 'NUM'
Copy all files of the archive to Doors:Num/

Place this text in your TEXT.WELCOME.USER :
======================  Not THIS line :) =====================
\#0Doors:Num/NUM1.01LOGIN\
================  Also not THIS line, but 1 up! :) ===========

Now place this text in your LANGUAGE file !
On line #924 .... :
        ~~~~
On line 924 you see this text :

\n1\q1Do you want to logoff the system (y/N)? \c7\?0

Well, erase this text, and type this instead of it :

\n1\q1\#0Doors:Num/NUM1.01LOGOUT

And now it MUST work! At least, at my BBS :)

5. Bugs
~~~~~~~
Well, I don't know if you can call it a bug...
When you logoff, and you DON'T want to leave a message,
you WON'T be asked if you want to leave a feedback,
but if you leave a message. then you will also be asked if
you want to leave a feedback... but I think most users
will leave a message... so they will also see the feedback
question.

6. Future 
~~~~~~~~~
Well, maybe there will be NUM v1.1 !
And now with or without the feedback question.. at both Y or N !

